## Superclaude Infrastructure

All agent infrastructure lives at `~/.claude/` (global). Project-local `.claude/` dirs are internal to those projects and must NEVER be modified by superclaude agents.

| Directory | Purpose |
|-----------|---------|
| `~/.claude/rules/` | Auto-loaded rules (numbered order) |
| `~/.claude/agents/` | Specialist agents (available via /agents) |
| `~/.claude/skills/` | Slash commands and agent-loaded skills |
| `~/.claude/plans/` | Cross-project orchestration plans and state |
| `~/.claude/comms/` | Spawn and outcome logs (`_spawns.log`, `_outcomes.log`) |
| `~/.claude/agent-memory/` | Persistent per-agent memory |
| `~/.claude/docs/` | Usage guide and historical references |

## Agent Hierarchy

| Level | Agent | Invocation | Role |
|-------|-------|------------|------|
| Strategic | Meta | `claude --agent meta` | Cross-project supervision, brainstorms with the user, writes plans, supervises w-* swarms. Never edits project code directly. |
| Worker | `w-merger`, `w-debugger`, `w-refactorer`, `w-reviewer`, `w-hostile-reviewer`, `w-planner`, `w-design-reviewer`, `w-implementer`, `w-doc`, `w-explorer`, `w-tester`, `w-committer` | Via Agent tool | Scoped specialist tasks |

A plain session with no `--agent` behaves as an ordinary Claude Code session with the rules loaded. `settings.json` is owner-run-only: no agent edits it.

### Workspace

Full protocol and canonical statement: `~/.claude/rules/12-agent-hierarchy.md` § Global Workspace Rule.

**All agents run from `<YOUR_WORKSPACE_ROOT>` as CWD** (e.g. `~/code/`); never `cd` into a project directory; use `git -C <absolute-repo-path>`.

## Key Rules (auto-loaded)
- `00-universal.md` — Read before edit, minimal changes, git discipline, stop conditions
- `05-coding-standards.md` — Language-specific standards (path-scoped)
- `07-language.md`: English for reasoning and chat; Italian for formal deliverables and code comments
- `10-orchestrator-protocol.md` — Plan/state protocol (in-project and superclaude)
- `12-agent-hierarchy.md` — Meta/Worker hierarchy, write scopes, workspace rule
- `15-programming-principles.md` — 10 programming principles (DRY, KISS, etc.)
